  "summary": "A steam trap automatically drains condensate (and air) from steam lines and equipment while holding back live steam. In the inverted bucket trap, steam entering under the bucket makes it float and close the valve; when condensate fills the bucket and the steam escapes through the small vent hole, the bucket sinks, opens the valve and condensate is pushed out — an intermittent cycle.",
